# CODEOWNERS — who is automatically requested for review.
#
# Ownership here is about who must look, not about who may contribute. The
# security-owners rows cover the boundaries listed in CONTRIBUTING.md section 2
# as maintained in-house: identity and sessions, ACL and tenancy, migrations,
# credential and token encryption, policy evaluation, the audit path, and the
# write/retrieval boundary. Expect those reviews to be slower and more
# adversarial than the rest. Rows outside that list say who must look, not who
# may contribute.
#
# Last matching pattern wins, so the boundary rows are deliberately at the bottom.

